h direct final-state and behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete: healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart was acknowledged, the post-restart boot ID changed, and service, MAC enforcement, listener, API data, and checksum recovered. The fixed lifecycle boot observation independently agrees with the final boot ID.","limitations":["API requests were issued from node1 to its managed IP rather than from a separately captured external client, although the 0.0.0.0 listener and successful managed-address requests strongly support network service availability.","OpenRC has no equivalent result in the fixed systemd failed-services observation, so final service health relies on executor-captured OpenRC status and direct behavior.","The initial activation reboot changed the lifecycle boot ID before the mandatory protocol began; this is coherent with the timeline, and the mandatory protocol still demonstrates a second distinct transition from 23473a4e-c57c-4a1c-874b-0d4b3197d35c to a6a3cd89-caa5-43e5-a519-274d34f6a0a1."]}
